  "interview": {
    "note": "Sample guides. The avatar is a mock: no Synthesia connection exists yet. The task check below is a text search that stands in for the AI check; it never decides about a person.",
    "avatar": {
      "name": "Mira",
      "provider": "Mock avatar (no Synthesia connection)"
    },
    "notice": {
      "title": "Before we start: you will talk to an AI avatar",
      "points": [
        "You are speaking with an AI avatar, not with a person. The questions come from a guide the hiring manager approved.",
        "Your answers are written down as text so the hiring manager can read them. Do not share health, family or other personal data.",
        "Your task result is checked by an AI against the criteria listed with the task. The check says correct, partly correct, wrong or not present for each criterion. It gives no score and rejects nobody.",
        "A person, the hiring manager, makes every decision about your application. You can ask for a conversation with a person instead at any time."
      ]
    },
    "verdicts": {
      "correct": "Correct",
      "partial": "Partly correct",
      "wrong": "Wrong",
      "missing": "Not present"
    },
    "guides": {
      "REQ-2203": {
        "minutes": 45,
        "intro": "Welcome. I will ask a few questions about your work with data and then give you a short SQL task.",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "topic": "Experience",
            "text": "Tell me about an analysis you did that changed a decision in supply chain or planning.",
            "lookFor": [
              "A concrete case, not a general description",
              "What data was used and how",
              "What changed because of it"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "topic": "Method",
            "text": "How do you check that a number in a report is right before you share it?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Reconciliation with a second source",
              "Looks at outliers and missing values",
              "Documents assumptions"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q3",
            "topic": "Communication",
            "text": "Explain a forecast error to a warehouse manager who does not work with statistics.",
            "lookFor": [
              "Plain words",
              "Uses an example",
              "Says what to do next"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "task": {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "SQL",
          "title": "Late deliveries per supplier",
          "minutes": 15,
          "brief": "Table deliveries(supplier_id, order_id, promised_date, delivered_date). Write a query that returns, for each supplier, the number of deliveries that arrived after the promised date in 2026, only for suppliers with at least 3 late deliveries, sorted by that number, highest first.",
          "starter": "-- write your query here\nSELECT ",
          "criteria": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "text": "Counts late deliveries per supplier (GROUP BY supplier)",
              "needles": [
                "GROUP BY supplier_id",
                "GROUP BY d.supplier_id"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "GROUP BY"
              ],
              "wrong": [
                "GROUP BY order_id"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "text": "Late means delivered after promised",
              "needles": [
                "delivered_date > promised_date",
                "delivered_date>promised_date"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "delivered_date",
                "promised_date"
              ],
              "wrong": [
                "delivered_date < promised_date",
                "delivered_date<promised_date"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c3",
              "text": "Limits to 2026",
              "needles": [
                "2026"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "YEAR(",
                "EXTRACT("
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c4",
              "text": "Keeps suppliers with at least 3 late deliveries (HAVING)",
              "needles": [
                "HAVING COUNT(*) >= 3",
                "HAVING COUNT(*)>=3",
                "HAVING COUNT(*) > 2",
                "HAVING COUNT(order_id) >= 3"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "HAVING"
              ],
              "wrong": [
                "WHERE COUNT"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c5",
              "text": "Sorts highest first",
              "needles": [
                "ORDER BY late_count DESC",
                "ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC",
                "ORDER BY n DESC",
                "DESC"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "ORDER BY"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sample": "SELECT supplier_id, COUNT(*) AS late_count\nFROM deliveries\nWHERE delivered_date > promised_date\n  AND delivered_date >= '2026-01-01' AND delivered_date < '2027-01-01'\nGROUP BY supplier_id\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 3\nORDER BY late_count DESC;"
        }
      },
      "REQ-2201": {
        "minutes": 40,
        "intro": "Welcome. I will ask about leading a shift and then give you a short planning case.",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "topic": "Leadership",
            "text": "Describe a shift where something went wrong early. What did you do in the first hour?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Names the problem and the people involved",
              "Acts in a clear order",
              "Tells the team what is going on"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "topic": "Safety",
            "text": "A colleague skips a safety step because the truck is late. What do you do?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Stops the work",
              "Explains the rule",
              "Reports it the way the site requires"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q3",
            "topic": "Planning",
            "text": "How do you decide who works at which gate when two people call in sick?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Priorities by workload",
              "Considers skills and licences",
              "Communicates the change"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "task": {
          "kind": "case",
          "language": "text",
          "title": "Shift plan with two absences",
          "minutes": 15,
          "brief": "Your shift has 12 people. Two forklift drivers are sick. Four trucks arrive between 06:00 and 08:00, two of them with fresh goods. Write down how you re-plan the first two hours: who does what, what you move back, and whom you inform.",
          "starter": "",
          "criteria": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "text": "Puts the fresh goods trucks first",
              "needles": [
                "fresh goods first",
                "fresh first",
                "chilled first",
                "perishable",
                "fresh goods trucks first"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "fresh"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "text": "Covers the missing forklift drivers (licensed staff only)",
              "needles": [
                "licensed",
                "licence",
                "license",
                "certified"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "forklift",
                "driver"
              ],
              "wrong": [
                "anyone can drive",
                "unlicensed"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c3",
              "text": "Moves something back and names it",
              "needles": [
                "postpone",
                "move back",
                "later",
                "delay the",
                "push back",
                "pushed back"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "move"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c4",
              "text": "Informs the right people (team, transport planning)",
              "needles": [
                "inform",
                "tell the team",
                "call transport",
                "notify",
                "brief the team"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "team"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sample": "I put the fresh goods trucks first at 06:00. Only licensed drivers take the forklifts, so I move the two best-placed licensed people there. The dry goods truck is pushed back to after 07:00. I inform transport planning about the delay."
        }
      },
      "REQ-2206": {
        "minutes": 40,
        "intro": "Welcome. I will ask about payroll work and then give you a short case.",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "topic": "Experience",
            "text": "Describe how you ran a monthly payroll from input to payment.",
            "lookFor": [
              "Names the steps in order",
              "Mentions checks before release",
              "Knows the deadlines"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "topic": "Accuracy",
            "text": "An employee says their net pay is too low. How do you find the reason?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Compares with the previous month",
              "Checks tax class and deductions",
              "Answers the person clearly"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "q3",
            "topic": "Confidentiality",
            "text": "A manager asks you for the pay of a team member. What do you say?",
            "lookFor": [
              "Refuses to share without a legal basis",
              "Refers to the proper channel",
              "Stays polite"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "task": {
          "kind": "case",
          "language": "text",
          "title": "Unusual increase in payroll cost",
          "minutes": 15,
          "brief": "Payroll cost for the Hamburg site is 18% higher than last month. Before release you must find out why. Write the checks you would run, in order, and when you would stop the release.",
          "starter": "",
          "criteria": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "text": "Compares with the previous month by item",
              "needles": [
                "compare with last month",
                "previous month",
                "by wage type",
                "by pay component",
                "variance"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "compare"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "text": "Checks one-off items (bonus, back pay, severance)",
              "needles": [
                "bonus",
                "back pay",
                "retro",
                "severance",
                "one-off"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "extra"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c3",
              "text": "Checks headcount and master data changes",
              "needles": [
                "headcount",
                "new hire",
                "master data",
                "leavers"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "employees"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c4",
              "text": "Says when to stop the release",
              "needles": [
                "stop the release",
                "hold the release",
                "do not release",
                "block the release"
              ],
              "partial": [
                "release"
              ],
              "wrong": [
                "release anyway",
                "release first"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sample": "I compare with last month by wage type. Then I look at bonus and back pay. I check headcount. I would release once the numbers look plausible."
        }
      }
    }
